{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>El ha-kodesh.</b> Corresponding to the Tent of Meeting." "<b>For in a cloud.</b> The reason he may enter only with incense, which makes a cloud, so that the Glory is not seen, lest he die. So its meaning is: I will not be seen by him except in a cloud. And some say that the meaning of \"for in a cloud\" is because I dwell in a cloud upon the kapporet, like the meaning of HaShem [said] \"to dwell in a cloud.\""], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:21.601215876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}